  "question": {
    "text": "An inductor of inductance <math> <mrow> <mn>2.0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow> </math> is connected across a charged capacitor of capacitance <math> <mrow> <mn>5.0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow> </math> and the resulting L-C circuit is set oscillating at its natural frequency. Let <math> <mtext>Q</mtext> </math> denote the instantaneous charge on the capacitor and <math> <mtext>I</mtext> </math> the current in the circuit. It is found that the maximum value of <math> <mtext>Q</mtext> </math> is <math> <mrow> <mtext>200</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math> When <math> <mrow> <mtext>Q</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>100</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C,</mtext></mrow> </math> what is the value of <math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>dI</mtext> <mo>/</mo> <mtext>dt</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow></math>?",
